---
/**
 * The working, below the verdict: what the policy itself does, what each of the
 * two do-it-yourself routes does, what the policy costs in friction, and how
 * fragile the whole thing is to the one assumption that is not a fact.
 *
 * WHY THIS IS ONE COMPONENT AND NOT FIVE CARDS. The old page scattered this
 * across an "Engine A" card, two "Engine B / C" cards, a bottom line, a
 * frictions X-ray and a sensitivity table — each with its own heading style,
 * and between them FOUR DIFFERENT QUANTITIES wearing the phrase "in today's
 * prices" (F-12). Two bold figures 500px apart shared a label while counting
 * different things, so a reader's first thought was that one was a typo. That
 * was not a wording defect: it was five surfaces each labelling its own figure
 * correctly, with nobody responsible for whether they could be told apart.
 *
 * So the frames are column headers over tables whose rows name their quantity —
 * T8's adjacent-columns pattern, which dd-019's own note says explicitly does
 * pass — and the phrase appears once per table rather than once per figure.
 *
 * THE THREE COSTS THIS SURFACE ADDED, all of them figures of zero typed in by
 * omission:
 *
 *  - the fund's expense ratio, which the growth route was not paying while the
 *    bond route's zero was a genuine fact (sol-028's fault a third time);
 *  - s.10(10D), which was assumed to exempt every policy whatever its cover;
 *  - an escalating income, which was priced as though it were level.
 *
 * Two of those favour the policy and one favours the replica. That is not a
 * balancing act — each was fixed because it was wrong — but it is the evidence
 * for dd-021 that the corrections were not all pointing one way.
 *
 * Design settled before the component in `InsuranceRoutes.checks.md`.
 */
import { SAFE_RATE_PCT, EQUITY_RATE_PCT } from '../../utils/insuranceInputs';

const cardClass =
  'rounded-2xl border border-navy-200 dark:border-navy-800 bg-white dark:bg-navy-950 p-5 sm:p-6 space-y-4';
const headingClass = 'text-base font-bold text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100';
const ledeClass = 'text-sm text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400 leading-relaxed';
const frameHeadClass = 'py-2 text-right text-sm font-semibold text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400';
const rowHeadClass = 'py-2 pr-3 text-sm text-navy-700 dark:text-navy-300 align-baseline';
const cellClass = 'py-2 pl-3 text-right text-sm font-bold tabular-nums text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100 align-baseline';
---

<div id="insuranceRoutes" class="space-y-6">

  <!-- 1. The policy, on its own terms. -->
  <section class={cardClass} aria-label="What the policy itself does">
    <div class="space-y-1">
      <h3 class={headingClass}>What this policy does</h3>
      <p class={ledeClass}>
        Everything you pay in, and everything it hands back, set against what those rupees will
        actually buy by the time they arrive.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="w-full text-left border-collapse">
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b border-navy-200 dark:border-navy-800">
            <th class="py-2 pr-3 text-sm font-semibold text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400">Over the whole policy</th>
            <th class={frameHeadClass}>in the rupees of each year</th>
            <th class={frameHeadClass}>in today's prices</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody id="policyLedgerRows" class="divide-y divide-navy-100 dark:divide-navy-900"></tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <p id="policyTaxLine" class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400 empty:hidden"></p>
    <p id="policyBreakEvenLine" class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400 empty:hidden"></p>
  </section>

  <!-- 2. The two replicas. Stacked at 375; side by side only when there is room. -->
  <section class="space-y-4" aria-label="The two do-it-yourself routes">
    <div class="space-y-1">
      <h3 class={headingClass}>Doing it yourself, two ways</h3>
      <p class={ledeClass}>
        Buy the same cover on the open market, invest what is left of each premium, and take out
        exactly what the policy would have paid you, in exactly the years it would have paid it.
        The only difference between these two is where the money in the middle sits.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
      <div class={`${cardClass} flex flex-col`}>
        <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3">
          <div class="space-y-0.5">
            <h4 class={headingClass}>The safe route</h4>
            <p class="text-sm text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400">Term cover, and government bonds at {SAFE_RATE_PCT}%</p>
          </div>
          <span id="safeBadge" class="shrink-0 px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-bold tracking-tight rounded bg-navy-100 dark:bg-navy-800 text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400">—</span>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-1 pt-2">
          <p id="safeLabel" class="text-sm font-semibold text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400">Left over at the end</p>
          <p id="safeFigure" class="text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-tight tabular-nums text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100">₹0</p>
          <p id="safeFigureReal" class="text-sm text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400">&nbsp;</p>
        </div>
        <p id="safeText" class="text-sm text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400 leading-relaxed pt-2">&nbsp;</p>
        <dl class="mt-auto pt-4 border-t border-navy-100 dark:border-navy-800 space-y-1.5 text-sm">
          <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-3">
            <dt class="text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400">Cover bought, over the paying years</dt>
            <dd id="safeRiskCost" class="font-bold tabular-nums text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100">₹0</dd>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-3">
            <dt class="text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400">Tax on the interest, as it was earned</dt>
            <dd id="safeTaxDrag" class="font-bold tabular-nums text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100">₹0</dd>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-3">
            <dt class="text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400">What the bonds charge to hold</dt>
            <dd class="font-bold tabular-nums text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100">₹0</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </div>

      <div class={`${cardClass} flex flex-col`}>
        <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3">
          <div class="space-y-0.5">
            <h4 class={headingClass}>The growth route</h4>
            <p class="text-sm text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400">Term cover, and an index fund at {EQUITY_RATE_PCT}%</p>
          </div>
          <!-- dd-007: two routes shown as equals. Only one of them used to carry a badge. -->
          <span id="growthBadge" class="shrink-0 px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-bold tracking-tight rounded bg-navy-100 dark:bg-navy-800 text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400">—</span>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-1 pt-2">
          <p id="growthLabel" class="text-sm font-semibold text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400">Left over at the end</p>
          <p id="growthFigure" class="text-2xl font-extrabold tracking-tight tabular-nums text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100">₹0</p>
          <p id="growthFigureReal" class="text-sm text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400">&nbsp;</p>
        </div>
        <p id="growthText" class="text-sm text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400 leading-relaxed pt-2">&nbsp;</p>
        <dl class="mt-auto pt-4 border-t border-navy-100 dark:border-navy-800 space-y-1.5 text-sm">
          <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-3">
            <dt class="text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400">Cover bought, over the paying years</dt>
            <dd id="growthRiskCost" class="font-bold tabular-nums text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100">₹0</dd>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-3">
            <dt class="text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400">Tax on the gains, as they were sold</dt>
            <dd id="growthTaxDrag" class="font-bold tabular-nums text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100">₹0</dd>
          </div>
          <!--
            THE ROW THAT DID NOT EXIST. A reader told the fund returns 12% and
            shown a balance built at 11.8% has been handed a figure that does not
            follow from a stated assumption (dd-009/dont-1). The fee is its own
            line, with the plan that produced it named.
          -->
          <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-3">
            <dt class="text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400">What the fund charges to hold</dt>
            <dd id="growthFeeDrag" class="font-bold tabular-nums text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100">₹0</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p id="routesTakeaway" class="text-sm text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400 leading-relaxed rounded-xl border border-navy-200 dark:border-navy-800 bg-navy-50 dark:bg-navy-900 px-4 py-3"></p>
  </section>

  <!-- 3. Where your premium actually goes: 3-Way Decomposition -->
  <section class={cardClass} aria-label="Where your premium actually goes">
    <div class="space-y-1">
      <h3 class={headingClass}>Where your premium actually goes: 3-Way Unbundling</h3>
      <p class={ledeClass}>
        Every traditional policy bundles three distinct cash flows behind one gross premium: pure life risk cover,
        distributor commissions & taxes, and net invested capital. Here is the exact decomposition of your annual premium.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Visual Decomposition Bar -->
    <div class="space-y-2 pt-2">
      <div class="h-3.5 w-full rounded-full bg-slate-100 dark:bg-navy-900 overflow-hidden flex border border-navy-200 dark:border-navy-800">
        <div id="decompBarMortality" class="h-full bg-sky-500 transition-all duration-300" style="width: 0%" title="Pure Protection"></div>
        <div id="decompBarFriction" class="h-full bg-amber-500 transition-all duration-300" style="width: 0%" title="Intermediary Friction & GST"></div>
        <div id="decompBarInvested" class="h-full bg-emerald-500 transition-all duration-300" style="width: 0%" title="Net Invested Capital"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between text-xs font-semibold text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400 gap-2">
        <span class="flex items-center gap-1.5"><span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-sky-500 inline-block"></span> Pure Cover (<span id="decompPctMortality" class="tabular-nums">0%</span>)</span>
        <span class="flex items-center gap-1.5"><span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-amber-500 inline-block"></span> Friction & GST (<span id="decompPctFriction" class="tabular-nums">0%</span>)</span>
        <span class="flex items-center gap-1.5"><span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-emerald-500 inline-block"></span> Net Invested (<span id="decompPctInvested" class="tabular-nums">0%</span>)</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <dl class="space-y-3 pt-2">
      <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4 border-b border-navy-100 dark:border-navy-900 pb-3">
        <dt class="text-sm text-navy-700 dark:text-navy-300">
          Pure Life & Health Protection
          <span class="block text-sm text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400">Open-market term cost for the same Sum Assured</span>
        </dt>
        <dd id="decompCostMortality" class="text-lg font-bold tabular-nums text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100">₹0</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4 border-b border-navy-100 dark:border-navy-900 pb-3">
        <dt class="text-sm text-navy-700 dark:text-navy-300">
          Intermediary Friction & GST Loading
          <span class="block text-sm text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400">GST on premium + agent commissions & administrative overhead</span>
        </dt>
        <dd id="decompCostFriction" class="text-lg font-bold tabular-nums text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100">₹0</dd>
      </div>
      <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4">
        <dt class="text-sm text-navy-700 dark:text-navy-300">
          Net Capital Actually Compounding
          <span class="block text-sm text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400">The actual portion of your annual premium working in the insurer's fund</span>
        </dt>
        <dd id="decompCostInvested" class="text-lg font-bold tabular-nums text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-400">₹0</dd>
      </div>
    </dl>

    <div class="pt-3 border-t border-navy-100 dark:border-navy-900 grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-navy-200 dark:border-navy-800 bg-slate-50 dark:bg-navy-900/50 p-3.5 space-y-1">
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400">Total GST over paying term</p>
        <p id="frictionGst" class="text-base font-bold tabular-nums text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100">₹0</p>
        <p class="text-xs text-navy-500 dark:text-navy-400">4.5% in year 1, 2.25% thereafter</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-navy-200 dark:border-navy-800 bg-slate-50 dark:bg-navy-900/50 p-3.5 space-y-1">
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400">Estimated Year 1 Commission</p>
        <p id="frictionCommission" class="text-base font-bold tabular-nums text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100">₹0</p>
        <p class="text-xs text-navy-500 dark:text-navy-400">Paid to distributor/agent</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 4. Sunk-Cost & Exit Arbitrage Matrix (for existing policyholders) -->
  <section id="insuranceSurrenderSection" class={cardClass} aria-label="Sunk-Cost and Exit Arbitrage Matrix" hidden>
    <div class="space-y-1">
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3">
        <h3 class={headingClass}>Sunk-Cost & Exit Arbitrage Matrix</h3>
        <span id="surrenderVerdictBadge" class="px-2.5 py-1 text-xs font-bold tracking-tight rounded-md bg-emerald-100 dark:bg-emerald-950 text-emerald-800 dark:text-emerald-300">Surrender & Reinvest</span>
      </div>
      <p id="surrenderLede" class={ledeClass}>
        You have already paid for some years. Surrendering triggers an immediate penalty under IRDAI Special Surrender Value (SSV) curves — but continuing may cost far more in lost compound growth.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Sunk Cost Summary Card -->
    <div class="rounded-xl border border-amber-200 dark:border-amber-900/50 bg-amber-50/50 dark:bg-amber-950/20 p-4 space-y-2">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-3 text-sm">
        <div>
          <span class="text-xs text-amber-800 dark:text-amber-400 font-semibold block">Total Premiums Paid</span>
          <span id="surrenderPaidToDate" class="text-lg font-bold tabular-nums text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100">₹0</span>
          <span id="surrenderYearsLabel" class="text-xs text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400 block">Across 0 years</span>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span class="text-xs text-amber-800 dark:text-amber-400 font-semibold block">Cashout Available Today (SSV)</span>
          <span id="surrenderValueToday" class="text-lg font-bold tabular-nums text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100">₹0</span>
          <span id="surrenderSsvFactor" class="text-xs text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400 block">0% of paid premiums</span>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span class="text-xs text-rose-800 dark:text-rose-400 font-semibold block">Immediate Sunk-Cost Loss</span>
          <span id="surrenderHaircut" class="text-lg font-bold tabular-nums text-rose-700 dark:text-rose-400">₹0</span>
          <span class="text-xs text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400 block">Surrender penalty</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- 3-Way Trajectory Comparison Table -->
    <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-navy-200 dark:border-navy-800">
      <table class="w-full text-left border-collapse">
        <thead class="bg-navy-50 dark:bg-navy-900">
          <tr>
            <th class="px-3 py-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400">Strategy</th>
            <th class="px-3 py-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400">Next Step</th>
            <th class="px-3 py-2.5 text-right text-sm font-semibold text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400">Final Wealth</th>
            <th class="px-3 py-2.5 text-right text-sm font-semibold text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400">In Today's Money</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="divide-y divide-navy-100 dark:divide-navy-800 text-sm">
          <tr id="surrenderRowOptA">
            <td class="px-3 py-3 font-semibold text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100">Option A: Surrender & Reinvest</td>
            <td class="px-3 py-3 text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400">Take SSV today + invest future premiums in index replica</td>
            <td id="surrenderOptANominal" class="px-3 py-3 text-right font-bold tabular-nums text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100">₹0</td>
            <td id="surrenderOptAReal" class="px-3 py-3 text-right font-bold tabular-nums text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100">₹0</td>
          </tr>
          <tr id="surrenderRowOptB">
            <td class="px-3 py-3 font-semibold text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100">Option B: Make Paid-Up</td>
            <td class="px-3 py-3 text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400">Stop paying; keep reduced policy payout + invest saved premiums</td>
            <td id="surrenderOptBNominal" class="px-3 py-3 text-right font-bold tabular-nums text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100">₹0</td>
            <td id="surrenderOptBReal" class="px-3 py-3 text-right font-bold tabular-nums text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100">₹0</td>
          </tr>
          <tr id="surrenderRowOptC">
            <td class="px-3 py-3 font-semibold text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100">Option C: Hold to Maturity</td>
            <td class="px-3 py-3 text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400">Pay all remaining premiums; collect full policy benefits</td>
            <td id="surrenderOptCNominal" class="px-3 py-3 text-right font-bold tabular-nums text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100">₹0</td>
            <td id="surrenderOptCReal" class="px-3 py-3 text-right font-bold tabular-nums text-navy-900 dark:text-navy-100">₹0</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <!-- Takeaway Banner -->
    <div id="surrenderArbitrageBanner" class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-emerald-200 dark:border-emerald-900/50 bg-emerald-50/50 dark:bg-emerald-950/20 text-sm leading-relaxed text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-200">
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 5. The one assumption that is not a fact. -->
  <section class={cardClass} aria-label="How fragile the comparison is">
    <div class="space-y-1">
      <h3 class={headingClass}>What if the market does not deliver {EQUITY_RATE_PCT}%?</h3>
      <p class={ledeClass}>
        The policy's income is a contract and the index fund's is not. Here is the same
        comparison at returns either side of the one assumed — and note that a lower return does
        not merely leave less over, it can mean the income stops arriving at all.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-navy-200 dark:border-navy-800">
      <table class="w-full text-left border-collapse">
        <thead class="bg-navy-50 dark:bg-navy-900">
          <tr>
            <th class="px-3 py-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400">If the index returns</th>
            <th class="px-3 py-2.5 text-right text-sm font-semibold text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400">Left over at the end</th>
            <th class="px-3 py-2.5 text-right text-sm font-semibold text-navy-600 dark:text-navy-400">Did it fund the promise?</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody id="insuranceSensitivityBody" class="divide-y divide-navy-100 dark:divide-navy-800"></tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class={ledeClass}>
      Each row is charged the same fund fee as the comparison above, so the rate in the first
      column is what the index does and not what you keep.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- 6. The shape of the whole thing, at a glance. -->
  <section class={cardClass} aria-label="The cash flow, year by year">
    <div class="space-y-1">
      <h3 class={headingClass}>The shape of it, year by year</h3>
      <p class={ledeClass}>
        Money out, then money back. The years of paying are the reason the comparison exists:
        that is when the alternative is compounding.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="relative w-full h-[250px]">
      <canvas id="cashflowChart" class="w-full h-full"></canvas>
    </div>
  </section>

</div>
